# This file exists to keep this directory in git. Do not remove it.
#
# The certificates are installed into this directory rather than committed, so
# the directory has to exist before they are written. Git does not carry an empty
# directory, so removing this file removes the directory with it.
#
# The amphora certificates, used when Octavia runs the `amphora` provider driver:
#
#     client.cert-and-key.pem
#     client_ca.cert.pem
#     server_ca.cert.pem
#     server_ca.key.pem
#
# They are deliberately not shipped as empty placeholders. Kolla's octavia
# precheck stats exactly these four names and fails when one is missing, and a
# zero-byte file satisfies that check -- so placeholders pass the precheck, the
# unusable files are copied into the service configuration, and Octavia instead
# fails at first use with `CertificateGenerationException: Unable to load PEM
# file`, leaving every load balancer in ERROR. Leaving them out lets the precheck
# fail instead, while the cause is still obvious.
#
# Generate them with the two commands below, which the deploy guide runs as part
# of bringing Octavia up:
#
#     osism apply octavia-certificates
#     osism apply copy-octavia-certificates
#
# https://osism.tech/docs/guides/deploy-guide/services/openstack
#
# The CA is keyed to `octavia_ca_password` in `environments/kolla/secrets.yml`.
# To check or renew an existing set, see "Octavia" in the troubleshooting guide.
